    "id": "distribute-pilot",
    "language": "In soccer, it's important to know who to pass to in which scenarios. Oftentimes, there can be multiple players who are available and open on your team that you can pass to. For example, these two players on my left, the str- the left striker and the right wi- and that player right there. However, some passes can be detrimental to your team's progression towards the goal. For example, if I were to pass to this player instead of our more or our higher player on the field right there, we could slow down our progression towards the goal and we could lose the impact of a turnover. It's always important to keep your head. As soon as you receive the ball, it's important to already have a picture of your surroundings. It's important to know the closest defender who will be shutting you down, as well as your options. Always look forward to your highest players. Those will be the players that will most progress you towards the goal. If these both players are covered, your second options are the ones horizontal to you. Creating one-two scenarios and building up is your other option there. However, because only one defender is blocking your pass to one of the strikers, we have a clear pass to this striker right here, and therefore, we will pass to him. So see, our defender approaches us. Who do we pass to? We already know our s- our scenario, our surroundings, and thus, we pass to this player right here.",
